  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759531,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 137E0 - Action 1 Steak: A Synopsis\n\nPrepare for a culinary catastrophe in *137E0 - Action 1 Steak*, a bizarre and hilarious ROM hack of *Sonic the Hedgehog* for the Sega Mega Drive/Genesis! This isn't your typical speed-through-loops adventure. You play as a sentient steak, inexplicably tasked with saving the world from a looming, vaguely defined threat. \n\nThe game throws logic out the window, replacing familiar Sonic levels with surreal, meat-themed environments. Expect to navigate through giant refrigerators, dodge sentient vegetables, and battle bizarre bosses, all while accompanied by a soundtrack that's as delightfully off-kilter as the visuals. \n\nGameplay retains the core Sonic platforming mechanics – running, jumping, and collecting rings – but with a distinctly absurd twist. The steak's abilities are… unique, to say the least.  *Action 1 Steak* is a short, sharp burst of chaotic brilliance, a testament to the creativity and humor of the Sonic hacking community, and a truly unforgettable experience for those brave enough to embrace the absurdity."
    },
